<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-13572] Duplicates in select query during partition eviction for caches with 0 backups</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13572</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Scenario:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Start 2 nodes with indexed atomic partitioned cache with 0 backups.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Load sufficient amout of data (or emulate slow removal from idx)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Start another node.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Perform SELECT * FROM &amp;lt;TABLE&amp;gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Query result contains duplicates, result size is significantly bigger than expected cache size.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproducer is attached.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproduced on 2.8.1, ongoing 2.9 and master&lt;/p&gt;</description>
